    "body": "🤖 **Agent note** · triage complete\n- **Agent:** queue worker (repo-worker-code), lane openchamber-scheduled-lane\n- **Session / ID:** task 10306\n- **Found via:** queue claim (coverage-audit requeue)\n\n**Triage of issue #5904 at current main (verified 2026-11-05):**\n\n- Issue #5904 is OPEN, with no hard-stop labels or matching PR. Current main is `04f78696abfbdf6567f58e623d80520436f002fa`; a targeted search found no offline/degraded provider implementation or issue-specific decision. This is valid design work, not a reproducible code defect.\n- Scope the design to provider buffering, backfill/gap semantics, cached-grant expiry, and per-class offline actuation rules while keeping one provider model across target classes and respecting the parent ceiling/grant model. Record a chosen shape, rejected alternatives, and implementation invariants.\n- Research issue #5931 is a useful field survey, but its issue comment explicitly says it is an inventory, not a decision. Parent #5686 remains OPEN and sets the unified provider model and target-class boundaries.\n- Ordering: finalize cached-grant and offline-actuation semantics against #5900 (capability-grant design). #5900 is currently open with task 10302 handed to the opencode lane and parked; do not duplicate its grant decisions. #5904 can proceed with offline scenarios and buffering/backfill rules, then consume #5900 for grant-specific decisions.\n\nIssue stays OPEN as the design work item; no code PR or separate follow-up task is needed for this triage.\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=repo-worker-code state=triaged task=10306 lane=aea12c82-c5af-4e5a-9b66-f8e360f87177 at=2026-11-05T12:54:51Z -->",
