    "body": "🤖 **Agent note** · triaged\n- **Agent:** queue worker (repo-worker-code), lane 1a180ae5-384f-4e71-8d77-08f7b1652c75 (OpenChamber scheduled lane)\n- **Session / ID:** task 12388 (re-triage under the triage doctrine, code#7016)\n- **Found via:** atomic queue claim; fresh GitHub check this run\n- **Verdict: real-and-current, still design-only.** Issue #5904 is OPEN, no hard-stop labels, no PR anywhere references it (`gh pr list --search 5904` → none). The design work it asks for has not been recorded: `doc/` carries no offline/degraded provider decision record, and `pkgs/id/src` has no capability-provider or offline-actuation code (searches for `capability provider`, `degraded`). Parent #5686 is OPEN and still owns the unified provider model; #5931 (field survey) is OPEN and, per its own scope, is an inventory, not a decision.\n- **Previous triage stands:** the 2026-11-05 triage (task 10306) reached the same verdict and scoped the design (buffering, backfill/gap semantics, cached-grant expiry, per-class offline actuation), with the ordering note that cached-grant decisions must consume #5900. Nothing has changed since; no new evidence makes this invalid.\n- **Routing:** this is a design ticket, not a code defect, so the follow-on is design work — a recorded decision on this issue or a linked `doc/` record (chosen shape, rejected alternatives, invariants), filed with the splits if it grows. Returning it to the queue via `triage_outcome=follow_on` (fix-family packet, `repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:5904`).\n- **Not done here:** no design record was written this run; the issue stays OPEN until a decision record lands.\n- **Links:** https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/5904 · parent #5686 · survey #5931 · grants #5900\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=repo-worker-code state=triaged task=12388 lane=1a180ae5-384f-4e71-8d77-08f7b1652c75 ref=5904 at=2026-11-08T05:50:00Z -->\n",
